      "url": "https://shelly-api-docs.shelly.cloud/gen2/Devices/Gen4/Shelly2PMG4"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus TCP must be enabled first (Modbus.SetConfig with enable=true, or in the web interface).",
    "The documentation lists input registers in 3xxxx notation: 33000 is input register 3000.",
    "Floats and 32-bit values are sent low word first, as in the documentation's modbus_cli examples (-B mixed).",
    "Each Switch component has a block of 20 input registers starting at 33000 + 20 x its id; Switch:1 starts at 33020.",
    "Not in this map: the output coils (the documentation lists them for the Pro 3EM with output add-on and the Pro EM only) and the Cover component, which has no Modbus register table. The Switch measurements are the same whether the channels are used as relays or as a roller shutter."
  ],
